# Deploy only when asked

**Do not** auto-deploy to Railway after routine coding, UX polish, presentations, docs, tests, or experimental work.

## When to deploy

Deploy **only** if the user explicitly asks (e.g. “deploy”, “ship it”, “make it live”) **or** they clearly need a production hotfix they just requested.

## Target (when deploying)

- Service: `edvidura-app`
- App URL: https://edvidura-app-production.up.railway.app
- Prefer the current feature branch; push only if the user asked to push / save to GitHub.

## Steps (only after an explicit deploy request)

1. Commit only if the user asked for a commit.
2. `railway up -s edvidura-app --detach` from the repo root (or the project’s documented command).
3. Confirm health: `GET https://edvidura-app-production.up.railway.app/health`
4. Tell the user the change is live (or failed) with the URL.

## Never auto-deploy

- Presentations, meeting boards, docs, rules, scratch scripts
- Teacher/student UX polish unless they asked to go live
- Incomplete or broken work
- Anything the user said to keep local
